{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300905-creating-experienced-characters-m20","id":1300905,"title":"Creating experienced characters M20","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-03-29T12:26:52-07:00","id":1300905,"title":"Creating experienced characters M20","content":"Greetings,<br /> <br /> I am planning on running a M20 game, the characters are a mix of adults and their teenage children, nephews and/or students, they awaken closely in game time.<br /> <br /> For the teenagers standard character creation seems fine, but the adults are quite experienced, I was thinking:<ul><li>Adults get 21 freebies but can only spend them on Attributes/Abilities/Willpower/Backgrounds/Merits.</li> <li>Limit adults to the starting mage &quot;template&quot;: Arete (1), Spheres (6).</li> <li>Teenagers follow the regular character creation in M20. (Justified as adults losing some of the wonder/potential by growing).</li> </ul><br /> Is there any guidelines to create experienced characters? Has the topic been discussed before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-29-2019, 04:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T14:25:23-07:00","id":1300949,"title":"","content":"V20 has a system which recommends certain amounts of EXP for different types of NPC. You just do the normal character creation, and then spend all the EXP. So an Archmage might have 1000 EXP on the sheet! An experienced Mage might have anywhere between 20 and 100 EXP added.<br /> <br /> For Player Characters, I recommend just using the same system for every character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T14:46:05-07:00","id":1300953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300905-creating-experienced-characters-m20?p=1300949#post1300949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 has a system which recommends certain amounts of EXP for different types of NPC. You just do the normal character creation, and then spend all the EXP. So an Archmage might have 1000 EXP on the sheet! An experienced Mage might have anywhere between 20 and 100 EXP added.<br /> <br /> For Player Characters, I recommend just using the same system for every character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, but how do you represent a character that awakens mid play? Sorry for the insistence, I am used to Mage the Awakening, and there is very easy to apply a template to a regular human to see what she becomes.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-29T16:39:42-07:00","id":1300978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300905-creating-experienced-characters-m20?p=1300953#post1300953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, but how do you represent a character that awakens mid play? Sorry for the insistence, I am used to Mage the Awakening, and there is very easy to apply a template to a regular human to see what she becomes.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean the PC starts as a sleeper, or the NPC starts as a mortal?<br /> <br /> I think it's simplest with an NPC to just start with the basic Mage sheet and buy stuff with the EXP.<br /> <br /> With a PC starting as a sleeper, just give them everything a Mage starts with minus Arete and Spheres. When they awaken mid-play give them Arete 1 and some Spheres for free (perhaps not all at once, but eventually six for free).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T05:39:10-07:00","id":1301062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300905-creating-experienced-characters-m20?p=1300978#post1300978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean the PC starts as a sleeper, or the NPC starts as a mortal?</div> </div> </div> </div>PC starts as a sleeper.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300905-creating-experienced-characters-m20?p=1300978#post1300978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a PC starting as a sleeper, just give them everything a Mage starts with minus Arete and Spheres. When they awaken mid-play give them Arete 1 and some Spheres for free (perhaps not all at once, but eventually six for free).</div> </div> </div> </div>That is what I am proposing for adults PLUS extra freebies. For teenagers I offer the regular creation (and therefore the possibility to raise Arete up to 3, and have higher spheres... A nice change of pace in which the adults have to learn from the youngsters).<br /> <br /> I am concerned about how to make starting sleepers mages, and how to make experienced characters BEFORE their awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T07:10:48-07:00","id":1301074,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300905-creating-experienced-characters-m20?p=1301062#post1301062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> PC starts as a sleeper.<br /> <br /> That is what I am proposing for adults PLUS extra freebies. For teenagers I offer the regular creation (and therefore the possibility to raise Arete up to 3, and have higher spheres... A nice change of pace in which the adults have to learn from the youngsters).<br /> <br /> I am concerned about how to make starting sleepers mages, and how to make experienced characters BEFORE their awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well if you want them to be experienced before they Awaken, the adult sleepers that is, then try this:<br /> <br /> For Attributes, One Primary set, two Secondary sets.<br /> <br /> For Abilities, One Primary set, two Secondary sets.<br /> <br /> 10 dots in backgrounds, to spend on things like Resources, Certification, Contacts etc.<br /> <br /> Basically help them build established connected adult characters. So, for example, Rowan the Accountant, who is also a local councilor (or equivalent for local government in setting). Knowledges Primary, the other two Secondary. Has dots in Law, Finance, Academics, Politics. His backgrounds include many Contacts (politicians, bankers, youth workers, people in the local media), a good income (Resources 3 or 4), and some Allies. He awakens, mid-game, into a Hypereconomic practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T14:58:35-07:00","id":1301158,"title":"","content":"The whole topic actually reminds me of something I wanted to make;<br /> Essentially, a Mortal/Sleeper/Person character sheet, and then addon-sheets for the various minor and major supernatural splats.<br /> <br /> While allowing modularity (i.e. a mortal becoming a supernatural later for example), it might also be possible to work up with rules for a sort of split chargen - first creating the original mortal side of a character, and then as a second step immediately creating the supernatural side.<br /> I just gotta figure out the exact rules that'd make that work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T15:26:35-07:00","id":1301166,"title":"","content":"So this may be helpful to design the &quot;template&quot; for a supernatural creature in WoD:<br /> The differences between a &quot;starting human&quot; and a &quot;starting mage&quot; are actually quantified in some places, but not everywhere (and not quite consistently, but these are what I usually see). Most of the time, OWoD gave humans similar stats to a starting nWoD/CoD character - 6/4/3 attribute spread and 11/7/4 Abilities. Mages (and most supernatural types) have 7/5/3 and 13/9/5, respectively, and usually two extra background dots (most mortals get five, though they also don't have to spend on Generation, Avatar, or other stats to represent a certain amount of power). If you wanted to, you could use that as your &quot;template,&quot; along with Arete, sphere dots, and the other perks of magehood. There is one hitch, of course - mortals also usually get about 6 more freebies - 21 to a supernatural's 15. However, you may wish to represent this difference by giving the mage two fewer dots in spheres when they awaken (which would be fitting thematically - the template at chargen is assuming a bit of training and practice, not just immediate talent), or by giving the humans just fifteen dots to start if they all are going to make the switch. Alternatively, if you do want your characters to have the extra &quot;heft&quot; as established individuals, leave the freebies and the benefits of Awakening as they are - the extra points can buy Attributes, Abilities, and Backgrounds that represent mortal ties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T05:22:44-07:00","id":1301279,"title":"","content":"Found something in the Book of Secrets for child mages... Essentially less freebies (10), more starting arete (2), limited physical attributes, mandatory flaws and merits... I might adapted this for teens. Close to my idea actually: youngsters get less freebies than an adult (in my idea adult got more), higher Arete","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-31-2019, 08:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T06:06:14-07:00","id":1301287,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1300905-creating-experienced-characters-m20?p=1301279#post1301279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Found something in the Book of Secrets for child mages... Essentially less freebies (10), more starting arete (2), limited physical attributes, mandatory flaws and merits... I might adapted this for teens. Close to my idea actually: youngsters get less freebies than an adult (in my idea adult got more), higher Arete</div> </div> </div> </div>I am running a game with Child Mages and ignored those rules because personally I preferred the idea of them starting at Arete 1 as a group and building up.<br /> <br /> With that said, the rules in BoS are definitely fitting for a normal Mage game; my table is setting the story in a school so starting at Arete 2/3 would have been a bad idea. Plus most of the players were inexperienced so Arete 1 means they learn the mechanics both IC and OOC.<br /> <br /> The True Faith presented as normal for child mages is interesting; good to ask the players what sort of faith the child has, and RP it either growing or fading away as they age.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T04:55:34-07:00","id":1301581,"title":"","content":"I've toyed with this idea many times but primarily for Vampire.<br /> What i usually do is to let me players create a regular mortal first, spend freebies etc and then add the template with whatever supernatural abilities the character needs.<br /> <br /> If it's regular character creation as in the characters start the game as non-mortal, i let them spend the extra attribute points and freebies on supernatural stuff to represent a few years as undead/awakened/etc.<br /> <br /> If they become supernatural in game i give them those freebies and supernatural dots at reduced XP cost for the first couple of session, to represent a freshly hatched newb that learns the ropes pretty quickly in the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}